{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Fire and hail, snow and vapor</b> — and all of them are from the earth, as is clear from the science of nature. And the fire — it is what kills by its scent, and likewise hail and likewise snow; vapor, and it is the exhalation that rises in the likeness of smoke, for it is hot. And storm-wind performs the word of HaShem in every place. Now, he has mentioned also these that are upon the earth, and afterward he mentioned —"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 148, :notes {0 "The text appears truncated at the end (the dash following 'and afterward he mentioned —'). 'האש, היא הממיתה בריחה' is read hyper-literally; בריחה could mean 'by its scent' or relate to ריחת (crackling); translated as 'by its scent' without smoothing. 'חכמת התולדת' rendered as 'the science of nature.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:08.310508555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}